Author:     Brendan Abolivier <brendan@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Tue Dec 9 12:47:32 2025 +0000
Commit:     Brendan Abolivier <brendan@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Tue Dec 9 12:47:32 2025 +0000

    Bug 1998426 - Queue outbound EWS requests. r=edicharry

    This patch introduces a request queueing system in ews_xpcom. A description of
    the queue's design has been documented in the header of `operation_queue.rs`,
    which is recommended as a starting point for reviewing this patch.

    As pointed out in this documentation, the approach used here introduces a bit of
    boilerplate and is less flexible than ideal. This is (hopefully) made a bit
    nicer by the use of macros, which are documented (with examples) in `macros.rs`.

    As part of introducing this queue, the actual request sending code has been
    factored out of `XpComEwsClient` into a dedicated structure, which accounts for
    the majority of this patch. Most file changes are very small and similar to each
    other as they adopt the new request handling logic. All this to say: this patch
    should be less scary to review than it looks :)

    This parch also introduces a few new dependencies, which are vendored in a
    separate (stacked) patch to ease review. This include two new direct
    dependencies (and a few transitive dependencies), which are `async_channel` and
    `oneshot`. The former provides an async MPSC channel which is used as the
    queue's inner buffer, while the former provides single-use SPCP channels which
    are used to share responses to EWS operations with the relevant consumers.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D274595

